# Reachability allow-list — symbols the application defines that are
# deliberately (or, for now, knowingly) absent from the linked image.
#
# Read scripts/reachability.sh first for the mechanism. This file is the
# policy, and the policy is a BASELINE FREEZE, not a blessing:
#
#   * every symbol here is absent from zephyr.elf today;
#   * a NEW absence — a function added with no caller — is not here, so the
#     build fails and someone has to decide;
#   * an entry that stops being absent is also an error, so this file cannot
#     rot into a rubber stamp.
#
# WHY A FREEZE RATHER THAN A CLEAN SHEET. This project shipped, in one
# session, a firmware-update orchestrator, a skyplot renderer, PTP Annex-P
# integrity, the whole Rb serial layer and about fourteen operator recovery
# actions — all written, all tested, all documented as delivered, and all
# discarded by --gc-sections because nothing called them. Host tests cannot
# see it: they link core/ directly and never touch the target image. Wiring
# them up took the absent count from 320 to 218. The remaining 218 are not
# all fine, and pretending otherwise by inventing a category for each would
# reproduce the exact failure this file exists to stop. So the ones with a
# defensible reason carry it, and the rest say TODO and are honest backlog.
#
# AUDIT STATUS — WHICH REASONS HAVE BEEN CHECKED AND WHICH HAVE NOT.
# The first version of this file assigned reasons in alphabetical blocks, and
# several of them were false. An adversarial audit went through it. What that
# audit reached, and what it did not:
#
#   AUDITED per symbol, against the linked image and the source:
#     inlined (10)     each one located in zephyr.elf — method below
#     no-caller (42)   reference set established for each; see that block
#     ATECC (18)       regrouped; the old blanket reason explained five of them
#     superseded (3)   the _profile twins confirmed present in the image
#
#   NOT INDEPENDENTLY AUDITED — the reason on each line is asserted, not
#   checked, and should be read as an untested claim:
#     fmt (18 of 18)   nobody has confirmed these are unreachable *because*
#                      they are host-side formatters rather than for some
#                      other reason. Plausible, unverified.
#     oracle (11 of 12) same. The twelfth, mp_cbor_rd_text, WAS checked — it
#                      had been filed under fmt purely because it sorts between
#                      two formatters, which is how the alphabetical-block
#                      mistake was caught in the first place.
#     ntske_* (6)      the deferral itself is verified (ARCHITECTURE.md §5,
#                      conf/net.conf); that these six are the complete set was
#                      not re-derived.
#     TODO (108)       declared backlog. Nothing to audit — that is the point.
#
# THE CATEGORIES:
#
#   fmt         enum->string formatters. The device logs numeric codes; the
#               names are for the host tool and for test failure messages.
#               NOT INDEPENDENTLY AUDITED.
#   oracle      the CBOR *reader*. This device is a CBOR writer — telemetry
#               goes device->host, the control plane is JSON-RPC. The reader
#               is how test_mp_stream.c and test_mp_mirror.c decode what the
#               writer produced and prove the round trip. NOT INDEPENDENTLY
#               AUDITED except mp_cbor_rd_text.
#   inlined     the instructions SHIP; only the separately-addressable global
#               entry point was collected. This is a strictly stronger claim
#               than any other category here — the others say "nothing calls
#               it", this one says "the code is in the image, at this address".
#               It is earned one of two ways and every line says which:
#                 (a) a .part/.isra/.constprop clone located at an address in
#                     zephyr.elf and called from a function that is itself in
#                     the image (GCC partial inlining); or
#                 (b) full inlining — a call site exists in the source, NO
#                     relocation anywhere in libapp.a names the symbol, and the
#                     enclosing caller is in the image; confirmed by
#                     disassembling that caller where the callee's work is
#                     small enough to recognise.
#               The caller-in-image check in (b) is the load-bearing one: it is
#               what separates "inlined into live code" from "referenced only
#               by other dead code", and dropping it is what would let a whole
#               dead subtree pose as shipped.
#   no-caller   the reference set has been established and it contains no
#               production caller: no relocation anywhere in libapp.a names the
#               symbol and no call site exists under app/ — or the only call
#               sites are inside functions that are themselves absent. The
#               named host suite is the sole exerciser. This is a FINDING, not
#               an absolution. It blesses nothing that TODO does not; several
#               of these are things an operator surface arguably ought to be
#               calling. What it buys over TODO is that the next reader does
#               not have to repeat the search.
#   deferred    a feature deliberately not enabled in this image, with the
#               reason recorded at the point of deferral.
#   superseded  a base variant whose _profile twin is what the engine calls.
#               Verified present in the image.
#
#   TODO        no decision yet. A standing action. Most of these are status
#               accessors that an operator surface arguably should be
#               reporting and does not — which is a gap, not a category.
#
# To regenerate the absent set after a build:
#   scripts/reachability.sh --update
# and then justify, or wire up, whatever it marks TODO.

